  "body_html": "<h1>$G$-equivariant sheaves and cosheaves</h1>\n<p>Assume $G$ acts cellularly on $X$ (see\n<a class=\"node-ref\" data-node-id=\"cellular_categories.cw_complex_setting\" href=\"cellular_categories_cw_complex_setting.html\">Locally finite regular CW complex with cellular G-action</a>).</p>\n<p><strong>Definition.</strong> A $G$-equivariant $\\mathscr{C}$-valued sheaf on $X$ is a pair\n$(V,a)$ where $V$ is a sheaf on $X$ and $a$ assigns to each $g \\in G$ a\nmorphism $a(g) \\in \\Hom(V, g^*V)$ satisfying $a(gh) = (h^* a(g)) \\circ a(h)$,\nwith $g^*V$ obtained by post-composing $V$ with $g : ]X[ \\to ]X[$.</p>\n<p><strong>Cellular form.</strong> Equivalently, a $G$-equivariant sheaf is a collection</p>\n<ul>\n<li>$V_F$, one object of $\\mathscr{C}$ for each cell $F \\in [\\![X]\\!]$;</li>\n<li>a restriction $r^V_{E,F} : V_E \\to V_F$ for each $E \\preceq F$;</li>\n<li>an isomorphism $a^V_{g,F} : V_F \\to V_{gF}$ for each $g \\in G$, $F \\in [\\![X]\\!]$,</li>\n</ul>\n<p>subject to four compatibilities:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>$r^V_{E,E} = \\id_{V_E}$;</li>\n<li>$r^V_{E,F} \\circ r^V_{D,E} = r^V_{D,F}$ for $D \\preceq E \\preceq F$;</li>\n<li>$a^V_{g,hF} \\circ a^V_{h,F} = a^V_{gh,F}$;</li>\n<li>$a^V_{g,F} \\circ r^V_{E,F} = r^V_{gE,gF} \\circ a^V_{g,E}$ (equivariance of restrictions).</li>\n</ul>\n<p>A $G$-equivariant cosheaf has the analogous data with restriction directions\nreversed.</p>\n<p><strong>Notation.</strong> We write $\\Sh_G(X,R)$ (resp.\\ $\\Cosh_G(X,R)$) for $G$-equivariant\n$R$-modules; for the trivial group we recover $\\Sh(X,R) = \\Sh_{\\{e\\}}(X,R)$.</p>",
  "proof_html": null,
